text:
If the leaf-fall's disasters make you pensive
that whirl and crackle along the broad boulevard;
if the north winds hint at you some vague anguish
and indistinct nostalgias and desires to weep;


if the luminous throbbing of the stars chills you;
if, incurably sad, you watch the Seine slide by,
and the reflection of scarlet lamps upon the river
seems to you the wake of some tragic vessel
where they carry the drowned from the Morgue to be buried;


Poor little one! Come with me: leave the barren bridges now.
There is a soul on these nights hostile to consumptives,
and a vampire disguised in a uniform who seeks sick women,
who courts those who cough and who, should you fall asleep,
will suck with a filthy trunk at your ivory nipples.
